        "at": "2026-11-11T02:06:31.586Z"
      }
    },
    "c16": {
      "anchor": "plain-card",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "",
      "excerpt": "",
      "text": "can we figure out a nice way to make the quotes overlap the bubble?  Maybe with a font with a prettier curly quote",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-11T02:00:10.440Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "card",
      "offset": 2,
      "edited": "2026-11-11T02:00:38.698Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-11T02:27:00.687Z",
          "html": "<p>Tried five ways, screenshots compared: Georgia's quotes at two sizes, Inter's, Libre Baskerville's, and Playfair Display's bold ones. Playfair's won: rounder, heavier marks. Offline it falls back to Georgia's.</p><p>C25 then moved them inside the pill's white, darker; C29 4px nearer its round ends.</p>\n<epic-net-effect><ul><li>Every quoted pill on both pages; the font is a Google Font loaded by <code>bubbly.css</code>.</li></ul></epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-11T02:06:33.707Z"
      }
    },
    "c19": {
      "anchor": "plain-to-test-card-setup",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "",
      "excerpt": "",
      "text": "italic?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-11T02:01:50.943Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "yes",
      "offset": 237,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-11T02:27:06.921Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes: <i>yes</i> and <i>no</i> are italic in steps, as are numbers (<i>12</i>, <i>300</i>) and texts. <code>yes or no</code> as a TYPE (<code>its \"lifted\" is yes or no</code>) stays upright.</p>\n<epic-net-effect><ul><li>Every value in a step; the rule is in C17's answer.</li></ul></epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-11T02:07:34.076Z"
      }
    },
    "c22": {
      "anchor": "solitaire-score",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "",
      "excerpt": "",
      "text": "too close!  should be 4px of white space between the purple line and the start of these bubbles",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-11T02:16:16.295Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "edited": "2026-11-11T02:17:10.990Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-11T02:27:13.507Z",
          "html": "<p>Done: 4px of white between a gutter and the band of a declaration inside its body (measured: 4.0px). Its words still line up with the body's lines.</p>\n<epic-net-effect><ul><li>Every nested band, both pages.</li></ul></epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-11T02:20:07.251Z"
      }
    },
    "c23": {
      "anchor": "solitaire-when-its-score-changes",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "",
      "excerpt": "",
      "text": "too far, add 4px back to the left of these lines",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-11T02:17:31.434Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "s",
      "offset": 163,
      "edited": "2026-11-11T02:17:35.917Z",
